@startuml campusclaw_tdd_agent_architecture
' Design baseline: pi-mono-java-design commit d2b9b4b6f4762e0e9734c144e3eb3273959e7e26.
' Code baseline: pi-mono-java commit ae0ae7c164b031afacd862794e8914243913f113.
' Source paths: modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/CampusClawAiService.java.
' Source paths: modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/loop/AgentLoop.java.
' Source paths: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeSessionController.java.
' Source paths: frontend/src/composables/useRuntimeApi.ts.
' Observed behavior at the recorded baseline: tests cover many modules, while CI runs only Maven verify and the legacy agent covers Runtime HTTP.
' Design reason: an independent Codex quality engineer must maintain product knowledge and tests while deterministic executors decide pass or fail.
' Pending implementation: recommended test-platform assembly; implementation evidence remains scoped to the baseline.

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
top to bottom direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 20
skinparam ranksep 35
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #64748B
}
title CampusClaw Quality Engineer - Target Structure
cloud "PR / Push / Design / Schedule" as Trigger
package "Knowledge" {
  artifact "Accepted designs / Source commits and diff" as Basis
  database "Capability registry\nRequirement / case / selector" as Registry
}
package "Independent quality engineer" {
  [TDD Skill] as Skill
  [Inventory Sync] as Inventory
  [Requirement and Risk Analyst] as Analyst
}
package "Deterministic platform" {
  [Impact Selector] as Selector
  [Domain Test Adapters\nJava / Contract\nDatabase / Process\nFrontend / Browser\nFault / Mutation] as Adapters
  [Evidence and Verdict Engine] as Verdict
}
package "Isolated maintenance and output" {
  [Test Maintenance Planner] as Maintainer
  [Failure Triage] as Triage
  node "Test worktree" as Worktree
  artifact "Test-only Draft PR" as PR
  artifact "Capability health report" as Report
}

Trigger -down-> Skill
Skill -down-> Inventory
Basis -[norank]-> Inventory
Basis -[hidden]down-> Registry
Registry -[hidden]down-> Skill
Inventory -[norank]-> Registry : version evidence
Inventory -[hidden]down-> Analyst
Registry -[norank]-> Analyst
Analyst -down-> Selector : required suites
Analyst --> Maintainer : coverage gap
Maintainer --> Worktree : tests / fixtures / registry
Worktree --> PR
Selector --> Adapters
Adapters --> Verdict
Verdict --> Triage
Registry -[norank]-> Triage : coverage state
Triage --> Report
Triage --> Maintainer : reproducible gap

legend bottom left
Pending implementation assembly; exact source evidence remains bound to recorded commits.
The registry is long-term product knowledge; chat memory is not authoritative.
Checked-in assertions decide results; the Agent explains and maintains tests.
Product code, weakened assertions and automatic merging are outside Agent authority.
endlegend
@enduml

@startuml design_to_test_maintenance
' Design baseline: pi-mono-java-design commit d2b9b4b6f4762e0e9734c144e3eb3273959e7e26.
' Code baseline: pi-mono-java commit ae0ae7c164b031afacd862794e8914243913f113.
' Design paths: pi-mono-java-manager-driven-multi-agent-runtime/chat-http-v1-design.md and pi-mono-java-tool-system/README.md.
' Test paths: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/test/java and modules/agent-core/src/test/java.
' Observed behavior: design versions and implementation tests evolve independently and exact requirement-to-test binding is incomplete.
' Design reason: mature requirements must create executable red tests before product implementation, while proposals must not block delivery.
' Pending implementation: recommended test-platform assembly; implementation evidence remains scoped to the baseline.

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
hide footbox
skinparam maxMessageSize 210
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantBorderColor #64748B
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  GroupBorderColor #CBD5E1
  GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
}
title Design-to-Test - Mature Requirement to Evidence
actor "Designer / Developer" as Author
participant "Quality Engineer" as Agent
database "Capability Registry" as Registry
participant "Maturity / Coverage Checks" as Gate
participant "Isolated Test Worktree" as Worktree
participant "Deterministic Runner" as Runner

== 1. Classify the changed requirement ==
Author -> Agent : Design or code change
Agent -> Registry : Refresh commits, hashes and source evidence
Registry --> Agent : Updated inventory
Agent -> Gate : Classify requirement maturity
alt research or proposed
  Gate --> Agent : Advisory only
  Agent -> Registry : Record target / open question
  Registry --> Agent : Advisory saved
  Agent --> Author : Non-blocking analysis
else accepted, frozen or implemented
  Gate --> Agent : Enforceable requirement

  == 2. Bind or create exact coverage ==
  Agent -> Gate : Resolve case and test selector
  alt Executable coverage exists
    Gate --> Agent : Selected tests
  else Coverage missing or stale
    Gate --> Agent : Coverage gap
    Agent -> Worktree : Add tests and fixtures
    Worktree --> Agent : Test patch and selector
  end

  == 3. Execute before reporting ==
  Agent -> Runner : Run selected mandatory suites
  Runner --> Agent : Results, logs and seed\nRed evidence for new behavior
  Agent -> Registry : Bind requirement / case / selector / run
  Registry --> Agent : Evidence reference saved
  Agent --> Author : Report + test-only Draft PR when needed
end

note over Agent,Runner
Accepted P0 without exact coverage fails the coverage gate.
Environment failure remains blocked; skip never becomes pass.
Test proposals require human review before merge.
end note
@enduml

@startuml realtime_and_scheduled_detection
' Code baseline: pi-mono-java commit ae0ae7c164b031afacd862794e8914243913f113.
' CI path: .github/workflows/ci.yml lines 4-26.
' Frontend paths: frontend/src/composables/useRuntimeApi.ts and frontend/src/projectors/runtimeEventProjector.ts.
' Observed behavior: pull requests and pushes run Maven verification, but frontend and deep environment suites are not required.
' Design reason: event-driven deterministic gates provide near-real-time detection, while Codex scheduled tasks perform deeper maintenance and triage.
